			},
			"date": "2025-05-22T15:25:28.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Not <u>really</u>.</p><p>It would be interesting to me to see a comparison where the WordPress instances only count installs that use a theme used by fewer than some arbitrarily low number of installations. I suspect the vast majority of WordPress users use WordPress primarily because they don't have to think about the code, that it's a fairly set it and forget it product. Which, no shade, but that skews the results.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
